(vector (map (:registry/operating-states (vector :intake :propose :approve :execute :audit)), (:registry/required-technologies (vector :robotics :identity :audit-ledger)), (:actor/scope-excluded-ops (vector :finalize-upholstery-operation :finalize-upholstery-execution-decision :declare-workshop-safety-cleared :declare-safety-clearance :override-shop-safety-officer-judgment :override-safety-officer-judgment)), (:actor/robotics? true), (:adr/related (vector "2799007319-cloud-itonami-isco-7319-handicraft-workers-nec-coverage" "2799007521-cloud-itonami-isco-7521-wood-treaters-coverage" "2799007317-cloud-itonami-isco-7317-handicraft-workers-wood-basketry-coverage")), (:adr/status :accepted), (:actor/scope-excluded-terms (vector "finalize the upholstery operation" "finalize the upholstery execution decision" "proceed with the upholstery execution" "authorize the upholstery execution" "declare the workshop safety cleared" "declare the workshop safety-cleared" "declare safety-cleared" "declare workshop-safety-cleared" "override the shop safety officer's judgment" "override the safety officer's judgment" "override shop safety officer judgment")), (:adr/id 2799007534), (:phase/rollout "{0 {:label \"read-only\", :writes #{}, :auto #{}}, 1 {:label \"assisted-logging\", :writes #{:log-work-record}, :auto #{}}, 2 {:label \"assisted-coordination\", :writes #{:schedule-crew-operation :coordinate-supply-order :log-work-record}, :auto #{}}, 3 {:label \"supervised-auto\", :writes #{:flag-safety-concern :schedule-crew-operation :coordinate-supply-order :log-work-record}, :auto #{:schedule-crew-operation :coordinate-supply-order :log-work-record}}}"), (:actor/domain :manufacturing/upholstery-workshop-scheduling-logistics-coordination), (:actor/proposal-ops (vector :log-work-record :schedule-crew-operation :flag-safety-concern :coordinate-supply-order)), (:actor/hard-checks (vector :upholsterer-verified :workshop-verified :effect-propose :op-not-allowed :scope-exclusion)), (:registry/maturity :implemented), (:actor/isco-08 "7534"), (:actor/always-escalate-ops (vector :flag-safety-concern)), (:adr/doc_type "adr"), (:operation/nodes (vector :intake :advise :govern :decide :request-approval :commit :hold)), (:operation/entry-point :intake), (:adr/body "# ADR 2799007534: cloud-itonami ISCO-08 7534 Upholsterers and Related Workers workshop scheduling/logistics coordination coverage\n\n## Status\n\nAccepted\n\n## Context\n\nThis is part of the occupation-classification track (sibling to the\n`cloud-itonami-isic-*` industry-actor rollout, same governing\nADR-2607121000): codify every ISCO-08 occupation unit group as an\nautonomous \"actor\" (LLM/advisor behind an independent Governor, a\n`langgraph.graph` StateGraph, append-only audit ledger), modeled on a\nrobotics premise -- a robot performs the occupation's physical/\nadministrative work, proposing actions to an independent Governor that\ngates them, never dispatches hardware itself, always escalates\nhigh-stakes decisions to a human. This ADR covers **ISCO-08 class 7534\n-- Upholsterers and Related Workers** only, Wave3 (production/trades)\nof the rollout (Wave0/1/2 100% complete, Wave3 batches 1-9 already\nlanded: 54 occupations before this one).\n\nThe `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's live `{:id \"7534\" ...}` entry\nwas verified against a fresh clone before any work began (`clojure -M\n-e \"(require 'kotoba.occupation) (println (kotoba.occupation/get-\noccupation \\\"7534\\\"))\"` from a checkout with the `kotoba-lang/\ntechnology` sibling present at the correct `../technology` relative\npath), and its `:name` read exactly \"Upholsterers and Related\nWorkers\" -- confirming the premise, no mismatch. Prior to this ADR the\nentry's `:maturity` was `:spec` with `:required-technologies\n[:robotics :identity :audit-ledger]` and no `:repo`/`:business-id`; no\nrepository existed at `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7534` (`gh api`\n404 confirmed before scaffolding). This ADR and its companion registry\nedit promote the `7534` entry to `:implemented`.\n\nISCO-08 7534 covers upholsterers and related workers, who use hand\ntools (staple guns, tack hammers, cutting knives) and handle padding/\nfoam materials -- a standard workshop hand-tool hazard, generically\ncomparable in shape to 7319's residual-category hazard profile\n(hand-tool injury, varied-material handling) rather than a single\ndominant technique-specific hazard like e.g. 7211's heat/molten-metal\nhazard. The controlling constraint for this vertical is that the\nclosed op allowlist must NEVER include any op that directly finalizes\nan upholstery-execution decision (e.g. deciding an upholstery job is\nfinished) or a workshop-safety-clearance decision (e.g. declaring a\nworkshop safety-cleared), nor override a shop safety officer's\njudgment -- those decisions must always be a hard permanent block,\nnever auto-commit-eligible. This actor is deliberately scoped to\nWORKSHOP SCHEDULING/LOGISTICS COORDINATION ONLY -- it never performs\nupholstery work or makes safety-clearance decisions itself.\n\nNo repository existed yet at `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7522`\n(Cabinet-makers and Related Workers, the closest-related workshop-\ncraft safety pattern by ISCO code adjacency) at the time this task\nbegan -- `gh api` confirmed 404 for that repo too, so the reference\nimplementation mirrored closely for module SHAPE and the\nclosed-allowlist + independently-verified-provenance safety pattern\nfell back to\n[`cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7319`](https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7319)\n(Handicraft Workers Not Elsewhere Classified: `store`/`advisor`/\n`governor`/`actor` split, `langgraph.graph` StateGraph, full doc set,\nalready landed and tested) -- cloned and read in full in this session.\nIts `deps.edn` `langgraph` git-sha pin was reused verbatim for this\nrepo, and its `craftcoord.*` namespace shape was renamed to\n`upholcoord.*` with `artisan`/`handicraft`/`craft` terminology\ntranslated to `upholsterer`/`upholstery` throughout.\n\n## Decision\n\nPublish `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7534` as an OSS workshop\nscheduling/logistics-coordination actor for upholstery workshops,\nfollowing the SAME governed-actor architecture as every prior\n`cloud-itonami-isco-*` actor in this fleet: **Upholstery Coordination\nAdvisor ⊣ UpholCoordGovernor** on a `langgraph.graph` StateGraph\n(`io.github.kotoba-lang/langgraph`, git-sha-pinned identically to the\nreference's `deps.edn` -- a different library coordinate from the\n`langgraph-clj` used by the unrelated `20-actors/*` actor family), with\nan independent Governor, human-in-the-loop approval via\n`interrupt-before`, and an append-only audit ledger.\n\nThis actor is deliberately **workshop scheduling/logistics\ncoordination ONLY, never direct upholstery-execution or\nworkshop-safety-clearance authority** -- it must NEVER be designed to\nexercise, simulate exercising, or propose exercising an\nupholstery-execution decision (e.g. deciding an upholstery job is\nfinished), a workshop-safety-clearance decision (e.g. declaring a\nworkshop safety-cleared), or any override of a shop safety officer's\njudgment. These are not merely gated behind escalation -- they are\nstructurally absent from the op-allowlist entirely.\n\n### Closed proposal-op allowlist (all `:effect :propose`)\n\n- `:log-work-record` -- job/commission/progress data logging\n- `:schedule-crew-operation` -- crew/task scheduling proposal\n- `:flag-safety-concern` -- surface a hand-tool-hazard/\n  material-handling-hazard/equipment-condition concern, ALWAYS\n  escalates, NEVER auto-commit eligible\n- `:coordinate-supply-order` -- padding/fabric/frame-materials\n  procurement proposal\n\nThis actor has **NO op, anywhere in its allowlist, that resembles** an\nupholstery-execution decision, a workshop-safety-clearance decision,\nor a shop-safety-officer-judgment override. These are **structurally\nabsent from the op-allowlist entirely**, not merely gated behind\nescalation -- an op such as `:finalize-upholstery-operation` cannot\neven be proposed by the reference mock advisor (its `infer`/\n`rationale-for` functions only ever emit one of the four allowlist\nops), and if any code path (a forged proposal, a future LLM advisor, a\nmisbehaving fork) ever produced such an op, the governor's\nclosed-allowlist HARD check (`:unknown-op`) rejects it unconditionally\nand permanently. A second, independent HARD check\n(`:scope-excluded-action`) names six concretely-forbidden ops\n(`upholcoord.governor/scope-excluded-ops`:\n`:finalize-upholstery-operation`,\n`:finalize-upholstery-execution-decision`,\n`:declare-workshop-safety-cleared`, `:declare-safety-clearance`,\n`:override-shop-safety-officer-judgment`,\n`:override-safety-officer-judgment`) as defense-in-depth, and is\nverified by dedicated unit tests\n(`upholcoord.governor-test/hard-on-scope-excluded-op-finalize-upholstery-operation`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-finalize-upholstery-execution-decision`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-declare-workshop-safety-cleared`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-declare-safety-clearance`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-override-shop-safety-officer-judgment`),\nplus a full-graph-run regression\n(`upholcoord.actor-test/holds-a-scope-excluded-op-even-at-high-confidence`,\n`.../holds-a-workshop-safety-clearance-op-even-at-high-confidence`).\n\n### Four HARD governor checks (permanent, un-overridable)\n\n1. **Upholsterer unregistered** -- any proposal must resolve to an\n   independently registered crew-member record (`:no-upholsterer`).\n   Never trusts the proposal's own claim of who the upholsterer is.\n2. **Workshop unregistered** -- any proposal must cite an\n   independently registered workshop (`:no-workshop`). Together with\n   check 1, this directly implements the CRITICAL invariant that a\n   worker/workshop record must be independently verified/registered\n   before any action.\n3. **Effect not `:propose`** -- any other `:effect` value is a HARD\n   block (a claim to directly actuate outside governance)\n   (`:no-actuation`).\n4. **Op not allowed / scope-excluded action** -- any `:op` outside the\n   closed four-op allowlist is a HARD, PERMANENT block (`:unknown-op`),\n   and independently, any proposal whose `:op` names one of the six\n   concretely-forbidden ops above, OR whose free-text `:rationale`\n   names a finalization/execution action for finalizing an upholstery\n   operation, declaring a workshop safety-cleared, or overriding a\n   shop safety officer's judgment, is a second HARD, PERMANENT block\n   (`:scope-excluded-action`), evaluated unconditionally on content --\n   defense-in-depth on top of the allowlist check: even if a future\n   change somehow widened the allowlist, content-based rejection still\n   independently blocks upholstery-execution/safety-clearance/\n   safety-override language wherever it appears in free text.\n\n### One always-escalate (SOFT) gate, one threshold gate, plus the general confidence floor\n\n- `:flag-safety-concern` -- ALWAYS escalates to a human, regardless of\n  confidence (governor's implicit always-risky check). This is the\n  ONLY channel by which the robot may surface a hand-tool-hazard/\n  material-handling-hazard/equipment-condition observation -- it never\n  resolves the concern itself, and the robot's role ends at \"here is\n  the hazard data,\" never \"here is what I recommend doing about shop\n  safety.\"\n- a `:coordinate-supply-order` proposal whose `:cost` exceeds\n  `supply-cost-threshold` (2000, inclusive boundary verified by\n  `ok-supply-order-at-threshold-boundary`) -- always needs human\n  sign-off, independent of confidence. This is an ESCALATION, not a\n  hard block, per the task's explicit domain design: an over-threshold\n  padding/fabric/frame-materials order is not itself unsafe, unlike an\n  upholstery-execution/safety-clearance/safety-officer-override\n  attempt, which is why it is handled by a different mechanism (soft\n  escalate vs. structural absence).\n- (advisor confidence below `confidence-floor` 0.6 also escalates, for\n  any op.)\n\n### Self-trip guard (fleet-known bug class, carried over from the sibling ISIC/ISCO tracks)\n\nA governor's scope-exclusion term list phrased as a bare noun (e.g.\n\"staple\", \"foam\", \"fabric\") can accidentally match inside the mock\nadvisor's own default rationale text for a legitimate proposal,\nself-blocking the actor's own happy path -- this is exactly the risk\nCLAUDE.md's worked example warns about for this task.\n`upholcoord.governor/scope-excluded-phrases` is phrased exclusively as\nfinalization/execution ACTIONS (e.g. \"finalize the upholstery\noperation\", \"declare the workshop safety cleared\", \"override the\nshop safety officer's judgment\" -- matching the task's own worked\nexample phrasing verbatim), never bare nouns, and\n`upholcoord.governor-test/default-mock-advisor-proposals-never-self-trip-on-scope-exclusion`\nis a dedicated regression test asserting every op in the closed\nallowlist, driven through the default mock advisor, never trips\n`:scope-excluded-action`. The mock advisor's own default rationale\ntemplate was deliberately written to contain the bare nouns (\"logged\nwork record for upholsterer ...\", \"scheduled crew operation for\nupholstery task ...\", \"... routed for shop safety officer review\")\nWITHOUT containing any of the full finalization-action phrases, so the\nregression test is a genuine stress test of the bare-noun-vs-\naction-phrase distinction, not a vacuous pass. Green on first run in\nthis session -- the scope-exclusion self-trip guard itself was never\ntripped during development.\n`upholcoord.actor-test/holds-a-scope-excluded-op-even-at-high-confidence`\nand `.../holds-a-workshop-safety-clearance-op-even-at-high-confidence`\nadditionally exercise the same invariant through the full graph run,\nconfirming a scope-excluded proposal never reaches `commit-record!`\nregardless of disposition path.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's `{:id \"7534\" ...}` entry\n  promoted from `:spec` to `:implemented`, with `:repo`/`:business-id`\n  set to the real repository\n  (`https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7534` /\n  `cloud-itonami-isco-7534`), and `maturity-summary`'s implemented\n  count bumped accordingly (recomputed live from the registry via\n  `kotoba.occupation/maturity-summary`, not assumed, immediately\n  before the edit).\n- Full test suite (`clojure -M:test`): 24 tests, 52 assertions, 0\n  failures, 0 errors -- raw output captured in this ADR's\n  `:test/counts` and in the task report, independently re-verified\n  against a brand-new fresh clone of the pushed repository (not just\n  the local working copy).\n- No `manifest/west.yml` changes -- this actor is registered purely via\n  the `kotoba-lang/occupation` capability registry, consistent with\n  sibling `cloud-itonami-isco-*`/`cloud-itonami-isic-*` actors.\n- No `kotoba-lang/technology` dependency was added to the actor's\n  `deps.edn` -- only the central `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry\n  itself depends on it, to resolve `:required-technologies` stacks.\n- This ADR is EDN-only, matching the live `90-docs/adr` convention\n  (commit `6d2d0eeda658`, \"Remove all .md, normalize ADRs to\n  tx-data\") -- a single-entity EDN vector with an `:adr/body` string\n  blob rather than a paired `.md`+`.edn`.\n\n## Alternatives considered\n\n- Giving the actor an op like `:approve-upholstery-execution` or\n  `:approve-workshop-safety-clearance` that is merely gated behind an\n  always-escalate list (the shape `cloud-itonami-isco-3313` uses for\n  `:approve-over-ceiling-posting`): rejected outright per the task's\n  explicit domain-design guidance -- an always-escalate op still means\n  the *capability* to finalize an upholstery-execution or\n  workshop-safety-clearance decision exists in the code path and is\n  merely deferred to a human gate. For a decision this severe (hand-\n  tool injury, padding/foam material-handling, workshop safety\n  clearance), the capability itself must not exist. The only op\n  related to shop-safety escalation is `:flag-safety-concern`, which\n  surfaces the need for human/shop-safety-officer attention and never\n  itself decides, authorizes, or defers an upholstery-execution or\n  workshop-safety-clearance decision for later automatic execution.\n- Making the supply-cost ceiling a HARD block (mirroring the 3313\n  reference's transaction-amount-ceiling HARD check): rejected per the\n  task's explicit domain design -- an over-threshold padding/fabric/\n  frame-materials order is not itself unsafe, so it is handled as a\n  soft escalate gate, not a hard block; only the upholstery-execution/\n  safety-clearance/safety-officer-override class is a hard,\n  unconditional block.\n- A bare-noun scope-exclusion term list (e.g. `[\"staple\" \"foam\"\n  \"fabric\"]`): rejected outright per the fleet-known self-trip bug\n  class described above (and CLAUDE.md's own worked example for this\n  exact task), and per the explicit instruction to phrase\n  scope-exclusion terms as finalization/execution ACTIONS, never bare\n  nouns -- this actor's own domain necessarily discusses staple/foam/\n  fabric/safety-officer concepts to do its scheduling/logging job, so\n  a bare-noun list would risk self-blocking the actor's own legitimate\n  proposals (regression-tested directly against rationale text that\n  deliberately contains those bare nouns).\n- Mirroring `cloud-itonami-isco-7522` (Cabinet-makers and Related\n  Workers) instead of 7319: rejected only because no repository\n  existed yet at `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7522` when this\n  task began (`gh api` 404 confirmed) -- the fallback reference\n  `cloud-itonami-isco-7319` was used per the task's own explicit\n  fallback instruction, and its generic workshop scheduling/logistics\n  coordination shape transferred directly onto upholstery's own\n  hand-tool/material-handling hazard profile without modification to\n  the governance architecture.\n- Merging `upholsterer` and `workshop` into a single entity (only\n  checking one provenance record): rejected -- the two-entity\n  provenance shape (independently-registered upholsterer AND\n  independently-registered workshop) matches the CRITICAL invariant\n  that a \"worker/workshop record must be independently verified/\n  registered before any action\" and the established pattern from\n  prior `cloud-itonami-isco-*` actors with two-sided provenance\n  checks.\n\n## Itemized safety confirmation\n\nEvery op in this actor's closed proposal-op allowlist, and why it is\nsafe under the constraints above:\n\n1. **`:log-work-record`** -- job/commission/progress data logging\n   only. Requires an independently registered upholsterer AND\n   workshop (`:no-upholsterer`/`:no-workshop`). Not an\n   upholstery-execution or workshop-safety-clearance decision in any\n   respect -- it is a records-management action.\n2. **`:schedule-crew-operation`** -- crew/task scheduling proposal\n   only. Cannot carry an upholstery-execution decision (structurally\n   absent from the op's field shape; any such attempt via free text is\n   caught by the `:scope-excluded-action` content check). Does not\n   authorize, finalize, or draw any conclusion about a specific\n   upholstery job -- it is a calendar/logistics action.\n3. **`:flag-safety-concern`** -- surfaces a hand-tool-hazard/\n   material-handling-hazard/equipment-condition concern to a human/\n   shop safety officer; ALWAYS escalates, unconditionally, at every\n   confidence level, NEVER auto-commit eligible. This is the ONLY\n   channel through which a safety observation may be surfaced, and it\n   explicitly never resolves, decides, or acts on anything itself --\n   the shop safety officer reviews and acts entirely on their own\n   authority.\n4. **`:coordinate-supply-order`** -- padding/fabric/frame-materials\n   procurement proposal only (item, cost). Not an upholstery-execution\n   or workshop-safety-clearance decision of any kind -- it is a\n   purchasing-logistics action, gated by ordinary cost-ceiling\n   escalation (above 2000 always escalates).\n\nNo op in this allowlist, and no op anywhere in this codebase, resembles\nan upholstery-execution decision (e.g. deciding an upholstery job is\nfinished), a workshop-safety-clearance decision (e.g. declaring a\nworkshop safety-cleared), or a shop-safety-officer-judgment override --\nthese categories are structurally absent, not gated, confirmed by: (a)\nthe closed four-op allowlist itself (`upholcoord.governor/allowed-ops`),\n(b) six concretely-named forbidden-op fixtures rejected at the\ngovernor-unit level (`upholcoord.governor/scope-excluded-ops`,\n`upholcoord.governor-test/hard-on-scope-excluded-op-finalize-upholstery-operation`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-finalize-upholstery-execution-decision`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-declare-workshop-safety-cleared`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-declare-safety-clearance`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-override-shop-safety-officer-judgment`),\nand (c) a content-based scope-exclusion check independent of the `:op`\nfield (`upholcoord.governor/scope-excluded-phrases`,\n`.../contains-excluded-phrase?`), tested directly against a rationale\nthat attempts to finalize an upholstery operation, declare a workshop\nsafety-cleared, or override a shop safety officer's judgment even via\nan otherwise-allowlisted op\n(`upholcoord.governor-test/hard-on-scope-excluded-rationale-even-with-allowlisted-op`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-rationale-declare-workshop-safety-cleared`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-rationale-override-shop-safety-officer`).\n"), (:adr/date "2026-07-18"), (:actor/cost-threshold-escalate-ops "{:coordinate-supply-order 2000}"), (:test/counts "{:total 24, :assertions 52, :failures 0, :errors 0}"), (:actor/coordination? true), (:actor/name "Upholstery Workshop Scheduling and Logistics Coordination Practice"), (:db/id -1), (:test/coverage (vector :governor-hard-checks :advisor-shapes :integration :store-contract :scope-exclusion-self-trip-regression :upholsterer-verification :workshop-verification :closed-op-allowlist :supply-cost-threshold-escalation)), (:registry/business-id "cloud-itonami-isco-7534"), (:registry/repo "https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7534"), (:adr/scope (vector :kotoba-lang/occupation :cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7534)), (:test/simulator :upholcoord.actor-test), (:adr/title "cloud-itonami-isco-7534 — Upholsterers and Related Workers Workshop Scheduling/Logistics Coordination Coverage"), (:adr/source-format "edn"), (:adr/references (vector 2607121000)), (:actor/id :cloud-itonami-isco-7534)))